    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nCouple of notes:\r\n- The 'mini.snippets' usage of `H.hide_completion()` is done before there is a guaranteed cursor move. Let's preserve this here, just in case. So just before `adjust_cursor()` (but probably still after `search()` as it is possible there'll be no movement) and before `pcall(nvim_win_set_cursor, ...)`.\r\n- In tests it is more informative to have `eq(is_pumvisible(), true)` just before typing a key to make a jump. This both makes a test more robust and shows test's intention more clearly.",
