        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": ">  ... before there is a guaranteed cursor move.\r\n\r\n I thought about that. However, is there a *guaranteed* cursor move? With treesitter, there is a `pcall`, and there won't be a movement if there is no target to jump to. Without treesitter, there is a check on `had_match`, after the jump.\r\n\r\n> ...  it is more informative to have ...\r\n\r\nYes, that indeed shows intention more clearly. Thanks.\r\n",
