        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> > ... before there is a guaranteed cursor move.\r\n> \r\n> I thought about that. However, is there a _guaranteed_ cursor move? With treesitter, there is a `pcall`, and there won't be a movement if there is no target to jump to. Without treesitter, there is a check on `had_match`, after the jump.\r\n\r\nThe `pcall` in tree-sitter is mostly to guard from edge cases. Like a position after the last line which is valid for tree-sitter nodes but not for placing cursor. The cursor usually moves there.\r\n\r\nAnd if there is no obvious difference or necessity of different order, making the as uniform decisions and code placement as possible usually helps in the long run. ",
