        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Would it be an idea to refactor the following lines that are duplicated in all new tests:\r\n\r\nI found that the threshold for wrapping common test steps in the wrapper to be used across several cases is usually higher than in the \"regular\" code. I.e. in regular code I'd agree that these lines would be a candidate for a separate function, but in tests I'd leave them as is. Creating a wrapper that leaves \"near\" tested code (i.e. `local validate = function() ... end` inside test case itself) is usually fine.\r\n\r\nThe reasons are mostly more direct error traceback (without extra last entry leading inside the helper function) and not having to write complex logic with lots of parameters.",
